WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:03.601
-He a three-time NBA champion,

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.567
and she is a two-time
New York Times

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.000
bestselling author.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.901
Together, they host
and executive produce

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.167
a new game show called
"About Last Night,"

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.901
which premieres
February 10th on HBO Max.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.801
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.067
Stephen and Ayesha Curry.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:20.834
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.934
Hey!

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.000
-Hello.
-Steph, Ayesha.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.467
Great to see you both.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.534
Thanks for doing this.
I appreciate it.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.234
I have some questions
for you guys,

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.868
because you've been married --

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.667
You've been married
for 10 years,

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.367
but you've known
each other for 20 years.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.133
You guys -- since your kids.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.667
-20?
-That's about true.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.133
We're getting old.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.000
-We're about to hit 20.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.033
-I want to know what your first
impressions of each other were.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.467
Ayesha, you can go first.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.467
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:48.901
-You know, it's so funny.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:52.901
I -- I was maybe 14 years old
when we first met,

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.868
and I just remember
thinking he was so cute

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.968
and my family being like,
"He looks like your brother."

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.334
I don't see it.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:03.968
For whatever reason,
every -- all of our family.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.801
Listen, we took 23andMe test,
we're in the clear.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.100
Everything's fine.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.934
-You're not brother and sister,
yeah.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.667
-We're not, no.
I don't see it.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.467
There was no rumors
about that going around, yeah.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.100
And Steph, what do you
remember about Ayesha?

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.567
-I mean, I knew she was
beautiful.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:20.300
We were both shy, so we didn't
know really how to, you know,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.968
talk to each other
and approach each other.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:24.234
But I also knew
she was from Canada,

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.467
and my dad played for the
Raptors for a little bit

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:27.467
when I lived up there.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.234
I love Canadian candy,

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.767
and so she was the candy plug
for a long time

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:33.367
before we even started.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.767
Just bring back candy
from Canada

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.501
and we'll get off
to a good start.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.901
-Yeah.

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:42.467
Ayesha, I heard that you had
a dating policy or something

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.834
where you wrote out a thing on
who you wanted

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:47.234
to be like your dream date,
and on the thing

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.968
it said no athletes.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.868
-It did in capital letters.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.434
I don't know why this was
a high school activity

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.434
that the theater teacher
had us do,

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.000
but she had us
write down

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.901
what we were looking for
in a significant other.

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.801
It was "High School Musical"
days.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:05.934
I was in my feelings,
and I wrote that on there.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.734
So it's like
one of those things

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:08.934
be careful what you say,

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.868
because God definitely
has a sense of humor.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.267
-[ Laughs ]
That is correct.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:18.534
Well, you've built this
giant culinary brand cookbooks.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:21.033
You sent me some awesome stuff,
by the way,

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.300
and I still use everything.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.434
You have food shows.
You have the magazine.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.934
No, it's amazing,
and you're brilliant.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.767
You're a great chef,
but on the basketball court,

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.701
Steph's nickname is Chef Curry.

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:35.133
Does that make you mad?

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:41.167
-It -- it makes me raise an
eyebrow because I just...

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.901
I get it.
He's cooking on the court.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.934
But like, I'm really like,

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.901
I'm -- I'm searing
steaks over here.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.567
-I'm actually cooking.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.734
-I don't get it, but we can --
we can share. It's fine.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.934
-Nah, we can't share.
You're giving that answer.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.267
I know happy wife, happy life.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.968
And we had this conversation
because Drake came up

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:01.868
with that line in his song,
you know,

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:05.067
Chef Curry with the pot,
and kind of took off from there.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:07.767
But the real Chef Curry
is Ayesha,

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.734
so I had to relinquish...

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.734
That nickname can never be used
for me inside the house.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.868
If it's fan base, cool,
they can use whatever.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.734
But she's the
real Chef Curry.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:18.734
-Ah, yeah.
That's the way to do it.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.434
[ Applause ]

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.734
Good man.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.834
Steph, I want to
congratulate you on --

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:27.801
you recently became the NBA's
all-time leader

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.234
in three-pointers made.

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.968
I mean...

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.868
you are officially the greatest
shooter in NBA history.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.234
I know you're very humble
about it,

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.534
but can we just talk about this?

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:44.133
President Obama disagreed
that -- with that sentiment.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.400
And do you want to clear it up.
-He did.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.934
He took a different spin on it.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:50.467
He -- obviously,
I have an amazing shooter

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.000
and teammate and Klay Thompson,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.868
and we won the Championship
back in 2015,

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.033
we went to the White House
to meet him.

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.934
And on the podium,
while we're, you know,

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.367
celebrating a championship
and the honor

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:04.000
of going to the White House,
he says,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.467
"You know, Steph,
I know you can shoot,

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:09.400
but I think Klay Thompson has a
much prettier form than you do."

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.234
And I said, "I can't -- I can't
disagree with you on that.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.067
If I was teaching
somebody how to shoot,

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.334
Klay has textbook form.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:17.467
-But...
-Yeah.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.634
-...you know, I always think

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:19.701
I'm the better shooter, so...

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.467
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:22.934
You got to call Barack back
and be like,

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.901
"Hey, you saw what I --
You saw what I did, right?"

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:26.234
Yeah, okay, yeah.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.868
I want to talk about your new
show, "About Last Night."

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.300
It is so fun.
It's a --

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.801
it's a game night
with celebrity couples.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:35.200
Ayesha, where did
the idea come from?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.367
-So, it's actually a reboot
of a show that aired

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.467
for like 10 seasons in the '70s
called "Tattletales,"

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:44.334
and it's just so light hearted
and fun,

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:46.634
gives you a little insight into,

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:50.267
you know, relationships that you
wonder about, but in a fun way.

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.767
And just with the -- with
this climate right now,

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.067
the world we're living in,
it's nice to just have something

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:57.367
where you can kind of just sit
down and have a good laugh.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:59.667
-I want to show everyone
a clip of the show.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.567
Okay, here is a sneak peek
of "About Last Night."

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:03.634
Take a look

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:05.634
-Who's better at dirty talk?

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.767
-Dang.
-Damn.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.501
Five for five?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:12.801
-God.
-Hold my things.

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:13.801
-We got you, we got you.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:14.934
Hold on, stay there.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:16.834
-Are you serious?
-You got that one?

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:17.868
-I got yours.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.667
-Y'all go five for five.

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.167
-Sheesh.
-We got all five right?

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:22.601
-All five of them.
-You got all five.

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:26.901
Which means you get extra five
for you charity.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.634
It must be the newlywed bliss.

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.767
-Yeah, it is.
Y'all go back upstairs, man.

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:32.367
Y'all get upstairs.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.100
-So, let's look
at these cameras off

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.767
and get the real party started.

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:38.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.400
-It's fun, it's fun.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.834
Stephen and Ayesha Curry,
everyone.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.767
"About Last Night"
begins streaming

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.434
February 10th on HBO Max.

